==Strategy==
This stage consists of only zombie enemies along with a curse cannon, preventing you from using crowd controllers. However, most decently ranged nukers are able to perform excellently in this stage, as their effects are not neutralized by the curse cannon, allowing them to deal high amounts of damage at a time with proper support and or meatshields. You can also do this by using high health anti-zombie ubers such as [[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat-8 Behemoth/Cat-10 Gigapult]], [[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aegis Garu]] or talented [[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)|Section Chief Gravicci]]. You can also use long-range attackers such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] along with meatshields like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] with research combos to counter all of the threats in this stage.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Theatre of Fear]] stages, Internal Scream is named after a horror movie, in this case ''[[wikipedia:Scream (1996 film)|Scream]]''.
*If your Battle Cats language is in Spanish then the name of the stage changes to "28 centuries later", it is a reference to a movie called [[wikipedia:28 Days Later|28 Days Later]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,500. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

